15. Qxe3 Qe7 16. O-O-O Kd8 17. f4 Nc6 18. Nxc6+ bxc6 19. Qxe7+ Kxe7 20. Re1+
Kd8 21. Nc4 Bb6 22. Ba4 Bd7 23. h4 Re8 24. Rhe2 Rxe2 25. Rxe2 c5 26. Bxd7 Kxd7
{Source: The Field, 11 April 1891 - "we are indebted to Mr Ure for the
following game, which was played on Board No. 1 in the Universities match" 
(The Field, 29 March 1891: "Mr J F Ure (Oxford) opened with a Scotch Game
which was tenaciously defended by Mr H E Atkins, the talented Cantab. It is to
be regretted that the score of the game is so indifferently recorded that it
is absolutely impossible to decipher it." (And yet someone seems to have
managed it subsequently - JS)} 1/2-1/2

