Ba5 {is wrongly given on Mega Database 2003}) 8. f5 (8. Nbd2 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5
10. Qb3 O-O 11. Qb5 Qd6 12. d4 exd4 13. O-O a6 14. Qa4 Nb6 15. Qb3 Na5 {
'and wins' is given as the game in the Sheffield Daily Telegraph, 1 Sep 1904,
but doesn't make much sense}) 8... d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Qb3 O-O 11. Qb5 (11.
Bxd5 Na5 12. Qb5 Qxd5 13. c4 (13. Be3 b6 {with a won game}) 13... Qd6 {Atkins
in the BCM}) 11... Qd6 {... "and White won" [BCM, but it is clear that Black
won] (Source: BCM, Oct 1904, p416). "The remainder is of no interest": source:
The Field, 3 Sept 1904. Note: Mega DataBase 2003 has the incorrect move 7...
Ba5 Perhaps we can guess that the game now continued as per the Sheffield
Daily Telegraph version of the score? Thus:} 12. d4 exd4 13. O-O a6 14. Qa4 Nb6
15. Qb3 Na5 {but this is pure speculation (JS). The game went on to move 30 or
so.} 0-1

