54. Qe3 $11 Nh4 $4 55. Qxg5+ {('and wins' Exeter and Plymouth Gazette, 20 Sept
1910)} Kh7 56. Qxh4+ {[The Times, 29 Aug 1910, gives this as the final move of
the game]} Kg7 57. Qg5+ Kh8 58. Kg2 a4 59. Qd8+ Kh7 60. Qe7+ {Sources:
Year-Book of Chess 1911, p112; Northampton Mercury - Friday 09 September 1910 
(complete score but incorrectly referring to Black as 'Dr F.S. Smith, London');
Manchester Guardian, 30 Aug 1910 (up to move 56: 'and White won'); Yorkshire
Post and Leeds Intelligencer, 27 Aug 1910 (up to and including move 43)} 1-0

