b6 15. Rd3 Bb7 16. Bxf6 gxf6 17. Rh3 Bc8 18. Rh4 Kg7 19. Qh5 Rh8 20. Qh6+ {
Source: Stockport Advertiser, 9 January 1914. The game source doesn't give
Atkins' opponent's forename nor the date of the match. Gerard Killoran points
to a reference in the Yorkshire Post and Leeds Intelligencer for 1 December
1913 which reports a Woodhouse Cup match in which Atkins defeated S Jackson -
who could be Sidney Jackson. Less probable is that Black was Maxwell Jackson 
(both Jacksons are documented at the Yorkshire Chess History website)} 1-0

